Package: hirdir
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: hirdir maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= @GLIBC@), adduser, ca-certificates, tzdata
Recommends: nginx
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: network equipment lifecycle and inventory platform
 hirdir is an inventory of the equipment, virtual machines, software and
 services a network operations team answers for, from the purchase request
 to disposal. It serves a web UI and a versioned API from one process, and
 keeps its records in SQLite.
 .
 This package carries its own Python interpreter and every Python
 dependency under /opt/hirdir. It installs a systemd service that listens
 on 127.0.0.1:8715, a daily backup timer, and nginx snippets that publish
 the service under a URL prefix on a site that already terminates TLS.
 Run hirdir-setup to add it to such a site.
